---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';

const { name, email } = SITE.owner;
const updated = '30 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Datenschutzerklärung</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Short version: this is a private hobby blog. It has no ads, no analytics and no tracking, and it doesn't
        share your data with anyone. The details are below.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        The person responsible for this website under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:<br />
        {name}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Visiting the website</h2>
      <p>
        When you open a page, your browser sends technical information to the server this site runs on: your IP
        address, the page you asked for, the date and time, and your browser type. This is needed to deliver the
        page to you (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, legitimate interest in running the website). The server does not keep access
        logs, and this information is not combined with any other data.
      </p>
      <p>
        All fonts, images and scripts come from this website's own server. No content is loaded from other
        companies, such as Google Fonts, unless you choose to play a video (see below).
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies. The only cookies are set by the comment
        system when you sign in to write a comment (see below).
      </p>

      <h2>Your crochet progress</h2>
      <p>
        When you tick off rounds in a pattern, your progress is saved in your own browser (so-called local storage)
        so it's still there next time. It never leaves your device and is not sent to the server. You can clear it
        with the "Clear all ticks" button on the pattern or by clearing your browser data. This storage is strictly
        necessary for the feature you asked for (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG).
      </p>

      <h2>Comments</h2>
      <p>
        Comments run on Remark42, a comment system hosted on this website's own server (comments.knittedstorybears.com).
        When you write a comment, the name you enter, your comment and the time it was posted are stored and shown
        publicly under the pattern. Remark42 keeps only a user ID, a user name and, if you sign in with an account,
        a link to your profile picture; the ID and name are stored in scrambled (hashed) form. To keep you signed in,
        it sets two cookies: a login token and a random security token. There is no tracking.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you choose to sign in with a Google account instead of just a name, Google shares your name and profile
        picture with the comment system. Google's privacy policy applies to that sign-in:
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is your consent when you post a comment (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). Comments stay online until you ask
        for them to be removed. You can download or delete everything the comment system knows about you from its
        settings, or email me.
      </p>
      <p>
        Comments written on the old Blogger version of this blog were moved here and are shown under each pattern,
        with the name the commenter used at the time. If one of them is yours and you'd like it removed, email me.
      </p>

      <h2>YouTube videos</h2>
      <p>
        Some patterns include a video hosted on YouTube (Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street,
        Dublin 4, Ireland). The video only loads when you press "Play video". It then loads from
        youtube-nocookie.com, and YouTube receives your IP address and information about your browser. Google may
        process this data in the USA. The legal basis is your consent, given by pressing play (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).
        Details:
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>
        Links to Instagram, Ravelry, Pinterest, Facebook or YouTube are plain links. Nothing is sent to those services
        until you click one; after that, their own privacy policies apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to access the personal data stored about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to
        restrict its processing, to receive it in a portable format, and to object to its processing (Art. 15–21
        GDPR). You can withdraw consent at any time, with effect for the future. Just email me at
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to complain to a data protection supervisory authority, for example the one in the
        country or German state where you live.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .updated {
    margin-top: 2.5em;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
